# S-843 T-958: ClassEnv parent-chain scoping (T-954) regression.
# A user class declared inside an inner dict scope is visible within that scope.
# The outer dict only sees its own scope — inner class declarations don't escape.
# Prelude classes remain accessible via the root parent frame in the parent chain.
# This test verifies that the class declaration is processed by the type checker
# without errors and that runtime evaluation still produces the correct output.
[
  # User class and instance declared inside a nested dict — scoped to that dict
  inner: [
    MyTag: [class [let MyTag a]
      tag: [Fn@String [a]]]
    result: [+ 10 5]
  ]
]

---

%.inner.result
=== out
Int(15)
